    "created_at": "2026-11-02T05:38:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-02T05:38:17Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the detailed report and session export, @RoboXGamer!\n\nI think this is a duplicate of #59339. In v2, the `doom_loop` permission is still accepted in config but nothing currently triggers it. So when a model keeps re-issuing the same tool call with the same input, as happened here with `skill` and `{\"id\": \"general\"}`, nothing stops the loop.\n\nPossible duplicates and closely related issues, ordered by likelihood:\n\n- #59339: v2 has no loop detection behind `doom_loop`, so repeated identical tool calls run indefinitely (same root problem)\n- #59567: assistant re-issues identical tool calls until it hits the output limit on v2 (already handled as a duplicate of #59339)\n- #46568: `Unable to load skill <name>` gives no hint when the name is a registered agent. This is the `general` agent/skill mix-up that started your loop.\n- #45442: an earlier report of a subagent looping on identical tool calls with no loop protection\n\nThere's also an open PR, #53032, which aims to stop repeated tool-call loops.\n\nThe bot will close this issue as a duplicate in 1 day unless you reply explaining how your problem is different.\n\n<!-- opencode-github-bot:reply:msg_938b81402e2e9e72d4356bc1750c32d52dc5e0629e4bac02247c355866ec28ba:close_as_duplicate -->",
